Topi Linkala <nes@iki.fi> writes:
> Hello,
> 
> does anybody know how to create player character monsters in wizard
> mode. I need to create some for debugging a patch I'm making.

If you just want a role-monster as a monster, you can ^G them up as
for any other monster; ask for an 'archeologist', 'barbarian', etc.

If you want an actual player-monster that's been created by
mk_mplayer() with all the appropriate equipment and stat adjustment,
that's a little trickier; you'll need to visit a special level that
will have them. The Astral Plane has an assortment, though those have
their own special checks throughout mk_mplayer(), or various Quest
levels if you need a more ordinary sort:

Knight Quest home (knights)
Samurai Quest locate and goal (samurai)
Wizard Quest goal (rogue and wizard)

For ordinary player-monsters of other classes, you're going to have to
alter a levelfile so that it creates one for you.

